@file ComparatorChallenges/ArnoldCounterexample.lean
@decl OAI.ArnoldCounterexample.main
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Counterexamples to stable-Morse and strong Arnold fixed-point bounds
-- L4DEL: intuition: The critical-number form of Arnold's fixed-point conjecture predicts at least as many fixed points as the minimum number of critical points of a smooth function. The formalized counterexample is a Hamiltonian diffeomorphism of the complex quadric threefold with exactly three fixed points, while every smooth function on that manifold has at least four critical points. At least one fixed point is degenerate. The separate nondegenerate Morse-number construction is not included.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Geometry.Arnold.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

