@file ComparatorChallenges/BufferedIsing.lean
@decl OAI.BufferedIsing.finite_graph_comparison
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Conformal universality for weakly interacting and random-bond Ising models
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalized result compares conditional Ising probabilities on finite graphs when two boundary mixtures differ but a common set of spins is pinned. If $q_0$ is the associated zero-field Fortuin–Kasteleyn connection probability after deleting the pinned vertices, the likelihood ratio lies between $\exp(-4\mathrm{artanh}\,q_0)$ and $\exp(4\mathrm{artanh}\,q_0)$. The statement allows arbitrary external fields and arbitrary probability mixtures satisfying the stated disjointness conditions. The paper's finite stopping-band approximation theorem is outside this selected statement.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Probability.Ising.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

