@file ComparatorChallenges/ComplexCancellation.lean
@decl OAI.ComplexCancellation.main
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Zariski cancellation and affine fibrations over the complex numbers
-- L4DEL: intuition: Affine-space cancellation asks whether $X\times\mathbb A^1\cong\mathbb A^{n+1}$ forces $X\cong\mathbb A^n$. The formalized result gives an explicit finite-type complex domain $A$ of Krull dimension four with $A[w]\cong\mathbb C[x_1,\ldots,x_5]$ but $A\not\cong\mathbb C[x_1,\ldots,x_4]$. Thus adjoining one variable erases a genuine algebraic distinction. The separate stable-coordinate and general line-bundle lifting consequences are not included.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Algebra.AffineCancellation.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

@file ComparatorChallenges/Conductivity.lean
@decl OAI.ScalarConductivity.main_nonuniqueness
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Joint metric and connection recovery from one boundary patch
-- L4DEL: intuition: The Calderón inverse problem asks whether boundary measurements determine an interior conductivity. The formalized result gives nonuniqueness for bounded measurable scalar conductivities on the ball $B(0,3)\subset\mathbb R^3$: two uniformly positive conductivities differ on a set of positive volume, equal $1$ near the boundary, and have the same full weak Dirichlet-to-Neumann operator. Weak solutions exist uniquely for every boundary trace.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.Conductivity.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

@file ComparatorChallenges/ConjugatePoints.lean
@decl OAI.ThreeManifold.main_theorem
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: A three-manifold without conjugate points or nonpositive curvature
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalized result separates absence of conjugate points from nonpositive sectional curvature. It constructs a closed connected orientable smooth three-manifold with a smooth Riemannian metric having no conjugate points, while the same manifold admits no smooth metric of everywhere nonpositive sectional curvature. The no-conjugate-points assertion ranges over all geodesics and tangent-bundle Jacobi fields, including constant geodesics and unbounded time intervals. The separate no-focal-points and CAT(0) consequences are not included.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Geometry.ConjugatePoints.ThreeManifold as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

