@file ComparatorChallenges/Cotype.lean
@decl OAI.Cotype.mainTarget_proved
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: The cotype–cotype conjecture under the approximation property
-- L4DEL: intuition: The cotype–cotype problem asks whether finite cotype of a Banach space and its dual characterizes $K$-convexity. The formalized result establishes this equivalence for every nonzero real Banach space with the approximation property: $X$ is $K$-convex exactly when both $X$ and $X^*$ have finite cotype.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.Cotype.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

@file ComparatorChallenges/CoulombCounterexample.lean
@decl OAI.Problem356.coulomb_counterexample_and_equal_infima
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Nonattainment of the three-marginal Coulomb Monge problem
-- L4DEL: intuition: The Monge ansatz asks whether an optimal multi-marginal transport plan can be induced by maps from one marginal. For the three-marginal Coulomb cost in $\mathbb R^3$, the formalization constructs a smooth compactly supported probability density, with smooth compactly supported square root, for which no pair of measure-preserving Borel maps attains the Kantorovich minimum. Nevertheless, the Monge and Kantorovich infima are equal: preserving maps with finite costs approach the minimum. This is the three-dimensional Coulomb result; the paper's inverse-power extensions in every dimension are outside this statement.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.CoulombTransport.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

