@file ComparatorChallenges/DukePrimeDegree.lean
@decl OAI.DukePrimeDegree.prime_degree_packet_measure_equidistribution_unconditional
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Torus-packet equidistribution in prime, quartic, and sextic degrees
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalization proves equidistribution of volume-weighted torus packets for totally real number fields of every fixed prime degree at least five. For any sequence of full lattices whose multiplier-order discriminants tend to infinity, the packet measures converge weakly to Haar probability measure and form a tight family, so no mass escapes. Arbitrary local homothety types are allowed, and the fields may vary along the sequence.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.NumberTheory.DukePrimeDegree.MainUnconditional as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

