@decl OAI.FKCRT.finite_fk_maps_converge_to_brownian_crt
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: The geometric phase diagram, diffusion, and spectra of random planar maps
-- L4DEL: intuition: For every fixed $q>4$, the formalization proves the Brownian continuum-random-tree limit for critical finite Fortuin–Kasteleyn planar maps. After rescaling graph distances in an $n$-edge map by a constant depending on $q$ times $n^{-1/2}$ and using normalized degree measure, the metric-measure space converges in distribution to the Brownian continuum random tree in the Gromov–Hausdorff–Prokhorov topology. The convergence holds through all positive integer sizes.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Probability.FKMaps.Convergence as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

