@file ComparatorChallenges/HalvingLines.lean
@decl OAI.PlanarHalving.power_bounds
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Power savings for planar halving lines and k-sets
-- L4DEL: intuition: A halving pair in an even planar point set is a pair whose line leaves equally many remaining points on each side. The formalization proves that some absolute $\varepsilon>0$ and $C$ bound the number of halving pairs by $Cn^{4/3-\varepsilon}$ for every sufficiently large even $n$ and every $n$-point set with no three collinear. It also proves a bound of the same form for all level-switch counts under the additional generic-position assumptions in the statement. The constants are existential.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Combinatorics.HalvingLines.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

@file ComparatorChallenges/HardSphere.lean
@decl OAI.HardSphere.condensation_with_mixed
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Positive-temperature Bose–Einstein condensation and exact quantum depletion
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalization proves ground-state Bose–Einstein condensation in the dilute hard-sphere gas. There are absolute constants $\varepsilon_0,c_0>0$ such that, whenever the density $\rho$ and hard-sphere radius $a$ satisfy $\rho a^3<\varepsilon_0$, the condensate occupation fraction has limit inferior at least $c_0$ along every thermodynamic sequence with $N/L^3\to\rho$. The bound covers every pure ground state, every mixed state supported on the ground space, and the normalized ground-space projection. It is uniform in the gas parameter within this range and concerns ground states, without a positive-temperature assertion.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.HardSphere.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

