@file ComparatorChallenges/HotSpots.lean
@decl OAI.StrictHotSpots.main_theorem
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: The hot spots conjecture for simply connected planar domains
-- L4DEL: intuition: The strict hot-spots conjecture asks whether extrema of a first nonconstant Neumann eigenfunction occur only on the boundary. The formalization proves the stronger interior statement on every nonempty smooth bounded simply connected planar domain: every nonzero eigenfunction in the first positive Neumann eigenspace has nonvanishing gradient throughout the interior. Consequently all global maxima and minima lie on the boundary. The conclusion applies to every eigenfunction even when the eigenvalue is multiple.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.HotSpots.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

@file ComparatorChallenges/HyperbolicCones.lean
@decl OAI.Paper256.main_result
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Hyperbolicity cones without semidefinite lifts
-- L4DEL: intuition: The generalized Lax conjecture predicts that every hyperbolicity cone is spectrahedral. The formalized counterexample is an explicit homogeneous polynomial of degree $20$ in $23$ real variables. It is hyperbolic, but its closed hyperbolicity cone cannot be represented as the positive-semidefinite region of any finite real symmetric linear matrix pencil, in any positive matrix size.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.HyperbolicCones.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

