-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalized result shows hardness of finding large independent sets even under a three-colorability promise. For every fixed $0<\delta<1/3$, a deterministic polynomial-time reduction maps binary 3SAT formulas to nonempty finite simple graphs. Satisfiable formulas produce three-colorable graphs; unsatisfiable formulas produce graphs whose largest independent set has fewer than $\delta$ times the number of vertices. The complete adjacency-matrix output is included in the runtime bound.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Combinatorics.IndependentSets.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

