@file ComparatorChallenges/IrrationalTriangleBilliard.lean
@decl OAI.TriangularBilliards.irrational_triangle_billiard
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Weak mixing of triangular billiards with an irrational angle
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalization proves that the unit-speed billiard flow in every nondegenerate Euclidean triangle with at least one angle irrational relative to $\pi$ is ergodic for normalized area times uniform angular measure. It constructs the flow outside the null set of exceptional trajectories, proves uniqueness of the flight chain there, and establishes measure preservation and the flow law almost everywhere. No genericity or Diophantine condition on the irrational angle is assumed.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Dynamics.TriangleBilliards.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

