@file ComparatorChallenges/LiebThirring.lean
@decl OAI.SharpLiebThirring.sharp_lieb_thirring
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Sharp finite-matrix Lieb–Thirring inequalities and all equality cases
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalized result determines the sharp one-dimensional Lieb–Thirring constant for $1/2<\gamma<3/2$. For every nonnegative $W\in L^{\gamma+1/2}(\mathbb R)$, it bounds the full negative-eigenvalue moment of $-d^2/dx^2-W$ by the one-bound-state constant times the potential integral. This constant is optimal and is attained by $(r+1)\mathrm{sech}^2(rx)$, where $r=(\gamma-1/2)^{-1}$. No finite spectral cutoff is imposed.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.LiebThirring.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

