@file ComparatorChallenges/LogConcaveQuery.lean
@decl OAI.LogConcaveSampling.exact_source_main
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Subpolynomial query complexity for log-concave sampling
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalized result determines the dimension exponent of exact value-and-gradient query complexity for well-conditioned log-concave sampling. For potentials with $V(0)=0$, $\nabla V(0)=0$, and $I\le\nabla^2V\le2I$, the least worst-case query budget achieving total-variation error at most $1/10$ is at most $C_\varepsilon d^\varepsilon$ for every $\varepsilon>0$, and at least $c\log d$ eventually. Hence the infimal polynomial exponent is zero. Algorithms may be measurable, randomized, and adaptive; arithmetic and bit costs are not bounded.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Probability.LogConcave.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

