@file ComparatorChallenges/MatrixRemoval.lean
@decl OAI.Problem348.no_polynomial_removal_bound
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Polynomial removal fails for ordered binary matrices
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalized result disproves a polynomial removal bound for one explicit $66\times66$ binary pattern. For every $c,C>0$, there is an $n\times n$ binary matrix at normalized edit distance at least $\varepsilon>0$ from being pattern-free but with fewer than $c\varepsilon^C n^{132}$ induced ordered copies. Row and column indices are independently increasing, and every zero and one entry must match. The construction gives an explicit sequence of such matrices, allowing edits in both directions.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Combinatorics.MatrixRemoval.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

