@file ComparatorChallenges/MetricEntropyDuality.lean
@decl OAI.MetricEntropyDuality.exists_entropy_duality_counterexample_with_covers
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: A counterexample to metric-entropy duality
-- L4DEL: intuition: Metric-entropy duality predicts a universal comparison between covering numbers of convex bodies and their polars. The formalized result disproves such a comparison: for every $a,b\ge1$, there is an origin-symmetric convex body $K$ in a positive finite dimension with $\log N(K,B_\infty)>b\log N(B_\infty^\circ,a^{-1}K^\circ)$, where $N$ is the least number of translates in a finite cover. A further construction makes the dual-to-primal logarithmic entropy ratio tend to zero as the dimension grows.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.MetricEntropy.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

