@file ComparatorChallenges/PolycyclicRecognition.lean
@decl OAI.PolycyclicRecognition.group_recognition
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Quasi-isometric recognition of virtually polycyclic groups
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalization proves quasi-isometric recognition of virtually polycyclic groups: every finitely generated group quasi-isometric to a finitely generated virtually polycyclic group is itself virtually polycyclic. It also realizes a finite-index subgroup of the recognized group as a uniform lattice in a simply connected solvable Lie group, which may differ from the original ambient group. The linked structural estimate controls the height-coordinate behavior of self quasi-isometries of the stated unimodular solvable Lie models, up to bounded error and one of finitely many linear height symmetries.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.GroupTheory.PolycyclicRecognition.Recognition as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

