@decl OAI.ReflexiveFixedPoints.exists_fixedPoint_of_canonicallyReflexive
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Nonexpansive fixed points in reflexive Banach spaces
-- L4DEL: intuition: The fixed-point question asks whether reflexivity suffices for nonexpansive maps on bounded convex sets. The formalized result gives an affirmative answer: every nonexpansive self-map of a nonempty closed bounded convex subset of a real reflexive Banach space has a fixed point in the original norm. Zero and nonseparable spaces are included, with no uniform convexity, normal structure, or weak-continuity assumption.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.Nonexpansive.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

