@file ComparatorChallenges/Rokhlin.lean
@decl OAI.Rokhlin.IsMixing
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Rokhlin’s multiple-mixing problem
-- L4DEL: intuition: Rokhlin's multiple-mixing problem asks whether ordinary mixing of one invertible probability-preserving transformation implies mixing of every finite order. The formalization proves this implication. For each $k\ge3$ and every $k$ measurable sets, the measure of their translated intersection tends to the product of their measures as all successive time gaps tend to infinity.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Dynamics.MultipleMixing.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

