@file ComparatorChallenges/SecondKahnKalai.lean
@decl OAI.LeanBlast.SecondKahnKalai.secondKahnKalaiBounds
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: The second Kahn–Kalai conjecture with an edge-count bound
-- L4DEL: intuition: The second Kahn–Kalai conjecture compares the threshold for a random graph to contain a fixed graph with its expectation threshold. The formalized result proves the comparison up to a universal factor times $1+\log_2|E(H)|$, and hence up to a universal factor times $\log_2 n$, for every graph $H$ with at least one edge and at most $n$ vertices, $n\ge2$. The bounds use the actual containment and expectation thresholds.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Combinatorics.GraphThreshold.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

