@file ComparatorChallenges/SquareDifference.lean
@decl OAI.SquareDifference.power_saving
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Power savings for intersective polynomial differences and prime arguments
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalization proves a fixed power saving for sets with no nonzero square difference. There are absolute constants $c>0$ and $C$ such that every $A\subseteq\{1,\ldots,N\}$ satisfying $a-b\ne m^2$ for all $a,b\in A$ and integers $m\ge1$ has $|A|\le C N^{1-c}$. The bound is uniform for every integer $N\ge1$.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Combinatorics.SquareDifference.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

@file ComparatorChallenges/SquareRootDegree.lean
@decl OAI.SquareRootDegree.main
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Boolean functions violate the square-root degree bound by arbitrary factors
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalization disproves the Gopalan–Servedio square-root degree conjecture by an unbounded factor. For every $C>0$, it gives a nonconstant Boolean function on a finite sign cube for which the sum of its linear Fourier coefficients exceeds $C\sqrt{\deg f}$, where $\deg f$ is its real multilinear degree. It also proves that the ratio of the sum of the absolute values of those coefficients to $\sqrt{\deg f}$ is unbounded among positive-degree Boolean functions.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Combinatorics.BooleanFunctions.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

