@file ComparatorChallenges/SteinitzBergstrom.lean
@decl OAI.EuclideanSteinitzBergstrom.main
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: The Euclidean Steinitz–Bergström bound
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalized result gives the Euclidean Steinitz–Bergström bound with one absolute constant $C$. For every finite family of vectors in the unit ball of $\mathbb R^d$, signs can be chosen so that every prefix in the prescribed order has norm at most $C\sqrt d$. When the vector sum is zero, a permutation makes every unsigned prefix satisfy the same bound. Repeated and zero vectors are included. The result is existential and does not supply an online algorithm.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.Steinitz.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

