@file ComparatorChallenges/StrongKadisonKastler.lean
@decl OAI.KadisonKastler.universal_strong_stability
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Strong Kadison–Kastler stability and its spatial boundaries
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalization proves the strong Kadison–Kastler conjecture uniformly. For every $\varepsilon>0$, there is a $\delta>0$ such that any two unital von Neumann algebras on the same complex Hilbert space at Kadison–Kastler distance below $\delta$ are conjugate by a unitary $u$ with $\lVert u-1\rVert<\varepsilon$. The tolerance depends only on $\varepsilon$, uniformly over the algebras, their representations, and the Hilbert space.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.KadisonKastler.StrongStability as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

