@file ComparatorChallenges/SubpolynomialLp.lean
@decl OAI.SubpolynomialLp.source_main
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Subpolynomial dimension reduction in Lp
-- L4DEL: intuition: For $p>1$, $p\ne2$, the formalization bounds the least dimension needed to embed every $n$-point subset of real $L_p$ with distortion $D$. For each fixed $D>1$, there is a constant $C=C(p,D)$ such that this dimension lies between $\log n/\log(1+2D)$ and $\exp(C(\log n)^{\gamma(p)})$ for every $n\ge2$, where $\gamma(p)=2-p$ for $p<2$ and $1-2/p$ for $p>2$. At distortion $1$ and $n\ge9$, it lies between $\lfloor(n-1)/4\rfloor^2$ and $\binom n2$. The least dimension is attained, and its logarithm divided by $\log n$ tends to $0$ for $D>1$ and to $2$ for $D=1$.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.LpDimension.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

