@file ComparatorChallenges/Superstring.lean
@decl OAI.Superstring.main
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: A factor-two approximation for shortest common superstring
-- L4DEL: intuition: The shortest common superstring problem asks for the shortest string containing each input string as a contiguous substring. The formalized result gives one deterministic polynomial-time algorithm whose output is a common superstring of length at most twice the unrestricted optimum. It applies to every finite list of explicitly encoded strings, with running time measured in input bits and the approximation ratio measured in symbol length.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
