-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Gigli’s characterization of Alexandrov curvature
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalization transfers a weak Hessian upper bound to every prescribed minimizing geodesic in an $\mathrm{RCD}(K,N)$ space with finite $N>1$. If a bounded globally Lipschitz function $F$ has weak Hessian bounded above by $G$ times the metric, where $G$ is bounded and continuous, then every constant-speed geodesic $\gamma:[0,1]\to X$ satisfies $(F\circ\gamma)''\le G(\gamma)\,d(\gamma(0),\gamma(1))^2$ in the distributional sense. Constant geodesics are included. The space is complete and separable with full support and measure finite on bounded sets; compactness and metric nonbranching are not assumed.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Geometry.WeakHessian.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

